From 8665aa9858dd136e07c134b89c5af59e854c7e3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:02:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Pickup-stall alarm's run re-places the cards it
 lists off the stalled machine

The alarm about machine M tells its run to re-place cards that cannot wait for M,
but the run had no supported way: worker shells are fenced from kanban move and
kanban_move(task_id=<other>) refused any card the run's own task did not create
(t_01a1cea829121562; the red sweep re-placed three by hand on 11-11).

kanban_pickup_stall_repin grants the alarm's own run kanban_move(task_id=<t>,
runs_on=[machine:<X>]) when every condition holds: the caller is an open alarm the
detector filed on M (M read from its pickup-stall:<M>: key); the alarm lists t (its
per-card key, a '- <id> (' body line, or a detector comment from M); t is ready,
unclaimed, has no run and is still pinned machine:M; runs_on is exactly one other
machine eligible now by the alarm placement rules (_takes_work: active, unheld,
copies cards, carries t's capabilities and profile; _ready_now: not draining, seen
recently, a free slot). A card another gateway created goes through the operator
call, which applies the same scope on its request side for an alarm caller.
Nothing reads or writes a registry hold. The hold and budget alarm texts and _tail
now name the supported command.
